- The directory for the ones not synced is gonna be `D:\My System\Local App Junction\`. In our case, it's `D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute` (I'll call it the Non-sync) for OmniRoute
- Phase 1: for `Sync/omniroute`, we're gonna copy the entire thing to the Non-sync. And then redirecting all the junction back to that new copy. Once we make sure the copy is working, we might rename the `Sync/omniroute` folder to something else, to make sure if the copy is working just fine. Then we can delete the `Sync/omniroute`
- Phase 2: for the `Sync/Config/omniroute` though. Things will rather be more complicated. We'll still gonna do it the safe way as Phase 1. Though we're gonna keep the following in the Drive synced folder:
``` 
│ storage.sqlite        │ 757MB │ ✅ YES - user data            │
├───────────────────────┼───────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ oauth/ (credentials)  │ 36B   │ ✅ YES - user data            │
├───────────────────────┼───────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ .env                  │ 140B  │ ✅ YES - user config          │
├───────────────────────┼───────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ db_backups/           │ 299KB │ ✅ YES - user backups         │
├───────────────────────┼───────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ omniroute_config_*.py │ 14KB  │ ✅ YES - config tools
```
=> In the non-synced. We add junctions pointing to the synced ones. 


